{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"competition","sourceId":125218}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/mubashirulhassan00/predicting-smartphone-addiction-s6e8-auc-0-96?scriptVersionId=341796627\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"<style>\n@keyframes glow{0%,100%{text-shadow:0 0 10px #7B68EE,0 0 20px #7B68EE}50%{text-shadow:0 0 20px #9B88FF,0 0 40px #9B88FF}}\n@keyframes slideUp{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)}to{opacity:1;transform:translateY(0)}}\n@keyframes shimmer{0%{background-position:-200% center}100%{background-position:200% center}}\n</style>\n\n<div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0f172a 0%,#1e1b4b 50%,#312e81 100%);padding:40px;border-radius:20px;border:1px solid #7B68EE;margin-bottom:20px;\">\n<h1 style=\"color:#e2e8f0;text-align:center;font-size:2.5em;margin-bottom:5px;animation:glow 3s ease-in-out infinite,slideUp 1s ease-out;\">📱 Predicting Smartphone Addiction</h1>\n<h3 style=\"text-align:center;font-size:1.2em;margin-top:0;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#7B68EE,#FF6B6B,#FFE66D,#4ECDC4,#7B68EE);background-size:200% auto;-webkit-background-clip:text;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent;background-clip:text;animation:shimmer 4s linear infinite;\">Playground Series — Season 6, Episode 8</h3>\n<p style=\"color:#94a3b8;text-align:center;\">Binary classification with AUC optimization · LightGBM + XGBoost + CatBoost Ensemble with Meta-Stacking</p>\n<hr style=\"border:1px solid #7B68EE;margin:15px 50px;opacity:0.4;\">\n<p style=\"color:#94a3b8;text-align:center;font-size:0.9em;\">\n🎯 <b>Target:</b> addicted_label (probability) · 📏 <b>Metric:</b> ROC-AUC · 🧠 <b>Key Trick:</b> Stringification of continuous features\n</p>\n</div>","metadata":{"_uuid":"4d3cb601-fe09-4607-88f7-91b77024cb4e","_cell_guid":"177ce353-de15-4d04-aa71-b839ff1a9194","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 📑 Table of Contents\n1. [⚙️ Setup & Configuration](#setup)\n2. [📥 Data Loading](#data-loading)\n3. [📊 EDA & Missing Value Analysis](#eda)\n4. [🛠️ Feature Engineering & The String Trick](#fe)\n5. [🤖 Multi-Model CV Training](#training)\n6. [🔮 Meta-Stacking Ensemble](#stacking)\n7. [📈 Diagnostics](#diagnostics)\n8. [📤 Submission](#submission)","metadata":{"_uuid":"42dc6e7a-f54d-46c7-91ee-69e27f680a8b","_cell_guid":"47a21b68-3bde-4270-bd3e-3c8bcd6a7578","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==============================================================================\n# IMPORTS\n# ==============================================================================\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport seaborn as sns\nimport os, gc, time, warnings\n\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder\nfrom sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score, roc_curve, classification_report\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n\nimport lightgbm as lgb\nimport xgboost as xgb\nfrom catboost import CatBoostClassifier\n\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\nprint('All libraries loaded.')","metadata":{"_uuid":"7d7a9778-c5a5-4251-9c30-32ace149b901","_cell_guid":"5d79223c-1f39-4971-b6d6-10b5c2a27a9f","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:04:53.22874Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:04:53.229Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:05:01.116358Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:04:53.228977Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:05:01.115714Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==============================================================================\n# CONFIGURATION\n# ==============================================================================\nclass CFG:\n    SEED = 42\n    N_FOLDS = 5\n    EARLY_STOPPING = 100\n    USE_GPU = True\n\nnp.random.seed(CFG.SEED)\nprint(f'Config: Folds={CFG.N_FOLDS} | Seed={CFG.SEED} | GPU={CFG.USE_GPU}')","metadata":{"_uuid":"e1e9a260-7a14-40c7-bfba-3d344a61984d","_cell_guid":"9b7827da-1014-458a-a7be-457b9951bbeb","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:05:01.117683Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:05:01.118264Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:05:01.124042Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:05:01.118238Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:05:01.122998Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==============================================================================\n# DATA LOADING\n# ==============================================================================\nINPUT_DIR = '/kaggle/input/competitions/playground-series-s6e8'\n\ntrain = pd.read_csv(f'{INPUT_DIR}/train.csv')\ntest  = pd.read_csv(f'{INPUT_DIR}/test.csv')\nsample_sub = pd.read_csv(f'{INPUT_DIR}/sample_submission.csv')\n\nTARGET = 'addicted_label'\n\nprint(f'Train shape: {train.shape}')\nprint(f'Test shape : {test.shape}')\nprint(f'\\nTarget distribution:\\n{train[TARGET].value_counts(normalize=True)}')\ntrain.head()","metadata":{"_uuid":"515a8216-7166-44f8-ae8e-73dede27801d","_cell_guid":"ee0f00ea-e2d9-4c0c-b5e8-24305c7b0ed3","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:05:28.682351Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:05:28.683178Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:05:30.516243Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:05:28.683147Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:05:30.51553Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==============================================================================\n# EDA — Missing Values & Feature Overview\n# ==============================================================================\nprint('Missing values (%) — Train vs Test:')\nmiss = pd.DataFrame({\n    'Train %': train.drop(columns=['id', TARGET]).isnull().mean() * 100,\n    'Test %':  test.drop(columns=['id']).isnull().mean() * 100\n}).round(2)\nprint(miss)\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(16, 8))\nfig.suptitle('Feature Distributions by Target', fontsize=16, fontweight='bold')\nnum_feats = [c for c in train.columns if c not in ['id', TARGET] \n             and train[c].dtype in ['float64', 'int64']]\nfor i, col in enumerate(num_feats[:6]):\n    ax = axes[i // 3][i % 3]\n    for label in [0, 1]:\n        subset = train[train[TARGET] == label][col].dropna()\n        ax.hist(subset, bins=40, alpha=0.5, label=f'{TARGET}={label}', density=True)\n    ax.set_title(col)\n    ax.legend(fontsize=8)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"_uuid":"077a956e-95d8-416c-a31c-79d9e2de9ee1","_cell_guid":"7f1eeee9-5ddd-4294-8922-3326a0ecf87e","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:05:33.626305Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:05:33.626693Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:05:35.835382Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:05:33.626666Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:05:35.834589Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==============================================================================\n# FEATURE ENGINEERING & THE STRING TRICK\n# ==============================================================================\n# The synthetic data has discrete grid patterns.\n# Converting continuous features to strings then target-encoding\n# reverse-engineers the generator's lookup-table logic.\n# ==============================================================================\n\n# Identify feature types\ncat_cols = train.select_dtypes(include=['object', 'category']).columns.tolist()\ncat_cols = [c for c in cat_cols if c not in ['id']]\nnum_cols = [c for c in train.columns if c not in ['id', TARGET] + cat_cols]\n\nprint(f'Categorical cols: {cat_cols}')\nprint(f'Numerical cols:   {num_cols}')\n\n# --- STRING TRICK: convert numeric features to string categories ---\n# This is the key insight from top competitors. We create string versions\n# of numeric features and then target-encode them. Tree models can then\n# treat each unique discrete value as a separate bucket.\n\ndef apply_string_trick(df, num_cols):\n    df = df.copy()\n    for col in num_cols:\n        df[f'{col}_str'] = df[col].astype(str)\n    return df\n\ntrain = apply_string_trick(train, num_cols)\ntest  = apply_string_trick(test, num_cols)\n\nstr_cols = [f'{c}_str' for c in num_cols]\nprint(f'\\nString-trick columns added: {str_cols}')\n\n# --- TARGET ENCODING for string-trick columns ---\n# Uses 5-fold OOF target encoding to prevent leakage\ndef target_encode_oof(train_df, test_df, cols, target, n_folds=5, seed=42):\n    train_df = train_df.copy()\n    test_df = test_df.copy()\n    global_mean = train_df[target].mean()\n    \n    skf = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=n_folds, shuffle=True, random_state=seed)\n    \n    for col in cols:\n        te_col = f'{col}_te'\n        train_df[te_col] = global_mean\n        \n        for tr_idx, val_idx in skf.split(train_df, train_df[target]):\n            means = train_df.iloc[tr_idx].groupby(col)[target].mean()\n            train_df.loc[train_df.index[val_idx], te_col] = (\n                train_df.iloc[val_idx][col].map(means).fillna(global_mean).values\n            )\n        \n        # For test: use full train encoding\n        full_means = train_df.groupby(col)[target].mean()\n        test_df[te_col] = test_df[col].map(full_means).fillna(global_mean)\n    \n    return train_df, test_df\n\nall_str_cat = str_cols + cat_cols\ntrain, test = target_encode_oof(train, test, all_str_cat, TARGET, CFG.N_FOLDS, CFG.SEED)\nte_cols = [f'{c}_te' for c in all_str_cat]\nprint(f'Target-encoded columns: {len(te_cols)}')\n\n# --- LABEL ENCODE original categoricals for tree models ---\nfor col in cat_cols:\n    le_col = LabelEncoder()\n    train[col] = train[col].astype(str).fillna('missing')\n    test[col]  = test[col].astype(str).fillna('missing')\n    le_col.fit(pd.concat([train[col], test[col]]))\n    train[col] = le_col.transform(train[col])\n    test[col]  = le_col.transform(test[col])","metadata":{"_uuid":"0be2a6dc-0724-442b-9502-9a1a5d27e10e","_cell_guid":"ed312da6-c010-445f-96db-5df208166319","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:05:35.836658Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:05:35.83699Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.102841Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:05:35.836967Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.101937Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==============================================================================\n# FEATURE SELECTION\n# ==============================================================================\n# Use raw numeric + label-encoded categoricals + target-encoded features\n# Drop the intermediate string columns (they were only for encoding)\n\nFEATURES = num_cols + cat_cols + te_cols\nprint(f'Total features for modeling: {len(FEATURES)}')\n\nX = train[FEATURES].copy()\ny = train[TARGET].values\nX_test = test[FEATURES].copy()\n\n# Replace inf with NaN (tree models handle NaN natively)\nX = X.replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan)\nX_test = X_test.replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan)\n\nprint(f'X shape: {X.shape} | X_test shape: {X_test.shape}')","metadata":{"_uuid":"6df7d2f2-ede6-4315-bf98-07b45eb52491","_cell_guid":"b6380992-31fc-4087-bbb0-00205b249c51","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.103961Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.104284Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.576728Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.104252Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.575844Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==============================================================================\n# CROSS-VALIDATION TRAINING ENGINE\n# ==============================================================================\ndef train_model_cv(model_type, X_tr, y_tr, X_te, n_splits, seed):\n    oof = np.zeros(len(X_tr))\n    test_preds = np.zeros(len(X_te))\n    scores = []\n    \n    skf = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=n_splits, shuffle=True, random_state=seed)\n    print(f'\\n--- Training {model_type} ({n_splits}-fold CV) ---')\n    \n    for fold, (tr_idx, val_idx) in enumerate(skf.split(X_tr, y_tr)):\n        Xf_tr, Xf_val = X_tr.iloc[tr_idx], X_tr.iloc[val_idx]\n        yf_tr, yf_val = y_tr[tr_idx], y_tr[val_idx]\n        \n        if model_type == 'LightGBM':\n            model = lgb.LGBMClassifier(\n                n_estimators=5000, learning_rate=0.02, num_leaves=63,\n                max_depth=-1, min_child_samples=20,\n                subsample=0.8, colsample_bytree=0.8,\n                reg_alpha=0.1, reg_lambda=1.0,\n                random_state=seed, verbosity=-1, n_jobs=-1\n            )\n            model.fit(Xf_tr, yf_tr, eval_set=[(Xf_val, yf_val)],\n                      callbacks=[lgb.early_stopping(CFG.EARLY_STOPPING, verbose=False)])\n            oof[val_idx] = model.predict_proba(Xf_val)[:, 1]\n            test_preds += model.predict_proba(X_te)[:, 1] / n_splits\n            \n        elif model_type == 'XGBoost':\n            model = xgb.XGBClassifier(\n                n_estimators=5000, learning_rate=0.02, max_depth=6,\n                subsample=0.8, colsample_bytree=0.8,\n                reg_alpha=0.1, reg_lambda=1.0,\n                tree_method='hist',\n                device='cuda' if CFG.USE_GPU else 'cpu',\n                random_state=seed, n_jobs=-1,\n                early_stopping_rounds=CFG.EARLY_STOPPING, eval_metric='auc'\n            )\n            model.fit(Xf_tr, yf_tr, eval_set=[(Xf_val, yf_val)], verbose=False)\n            oof[val_idx] = model.predict_proba(Xf_val)[:, 1]\n            test_preds += model.predict_proba(X_te)[:, 1] / n_splits\n            \n        elif model_type == 'CatBoost':\n            model = CatBoostClassifier(\n                iterations=5000, learning_rate=0.02, depth=6,\n                l2_leaf_reg=3.0, random_seed=seed,\n                task_type='GPU' if CFG.USE_GPU else 'CPU',\n                verbose=0, early_stopping_rounds=CFG.EARLY_STOPPING,\n                eval_metric='AUC'\n            )\n            model.fit(Xf_tr, yf_tr, eval_set=(Xf_val, yf_val))\n            oof[val_idx] = model.predict_proba(Xf_val)[:, 1]\n            test_preds += model.predict_proba(X_te)[:, 1] / n_splits\n        \n        fold_auc = roc_auc_score(yf_val, oof[val_idx])\n        scores.append(fold_auc)\n        print(f'  Fold {fold+1} AUC: {fold_auc:.6f}')\n    \n    overall_auc = roc_auc_score(y_tr, oof)\n    print(f'  Overall OOF AUC: {overall_auc:.6f} (std: {np.std(scores):.6f})')\n    return oof, test_preds, overall_auc","metadata":{"_uuid":"d7b81a96-67d5-4f40-beeb-ddc390c52545","_cell_guid":"b26a4891-a08e-4a5b-93ae-09ad8c303453","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.579229Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.579477Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.591822Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.579456Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.590176Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"lgb_oof, lgb_test, lgb_auc = train_model_cv('LightGBM', X, y, X_test, CFG.N_FOLDS, CFG.SEED)","metadata":{"_uuid":"c6ec3ae6-ee43-43d6-8cc3-14a5e5849ff7","_cell_guid":"bb26a0ce-3697-49bc-a334-3e001640d9c2","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.593021Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.593343Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:20:17.744285Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:06:03.593323Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:20:17.743574Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"xgb_oof, xgb_test, xgb_auc = train_model_cv('XGBoost', X, y, X_test, CFG.N_FOLDS, CFG.SEED + 1)","metadata":{"_uuid":"c063e76a-f1fe-4f7b-874e-8ac8f69f212e","_cell_guid":"546ac53f-0fac-4844-be1b-63113a6bb2c6","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:20:17.745441Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:20:17.745839Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:22:22.299431Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:20:17.745802Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:22:22.298842Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"cat_oof, cat_test, cat_auc = train_model_cv('CatBoost', X, y, X_test, CFG.N_FOLDS, CFG.SEED + 2)","metadata":{"_uuid":"f0142191-d3ec-4c93-b495-699d51ca68ce","_cell_guid":"7e464e45-8ce3-4083-aad9-010672fd40bd","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:22:22.301013Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:22:22.301326Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:26:45.522109Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:22:22.301304Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:26:45.521227Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==============================================================================\n# META-STACKING ENSEMBLE\n# ==============================================================================\n# Use OOF predictions from base models as features for a meta-learner.\n# This is the approach that top competitors use for maximum generalization.\n# A simple Logistic Regression meta-learner prevents overfitting.\n# ==============================================================================\nprint('\\n--- Building Meta-Stacking Ensemble ---')\n\n# Stack OOF predictions\nmeta_train = np.column_stack([lgb_oof, xgb_oof, cat_oof])\nmeta_test  = np.column_stack([lgb_test, xgb_test, cat_test])\n\n# Add polynomial interaction features between OOF predictions\nmeta_train_poly = np.column_stack([\n    meta_train,\n    lgb_oof * xgb_oof,\n    lgb_oof * cat_oof,\n    xgb_oof * cat_oof,\n])\nmeta_test_poly = np.column_stack([\n    meta_test,\n    lgb_test * xgb_test,\n    lgb_test * cat_test,\n    xgb_test * cat_test,\n])\n\n# Meta-learner: Logistic Regression (simple, low variance)\nmeta_oof = np.zeros(len(meta_train_poly))\nmeta_test_preds = np.zeros(len(meta_test_poly))\nmeta_scores = []\n\nskf_meta = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=CFG.N_FOLDS, shuffle=True, random_state=CFG.SEED)\nfor fold, (tr_idx, val_idx) in enumerate(skf_meta.split(meta_train_poly, y)):\n    lr = LogisticRegression(C=1.0, max_iter=1000, random_state=CFG.SEED)\n    lr.fit(meta_train_poly[tr_idx], y[tr_idx])\n    meta_oof[val_idx] = lr.predict_proba(meta_train_poly[val_idx])[:, 1]\n    meta_test_preds += lr.predict_proba(meta_test_poly)[:, 1] / CFG.N_FOLDS\n    fold_auc = roc_auc_score(y[val_idx], meta_oof[val_idx])\n    meta_scores.append(fold_auc)\n    print(f'  Meta Fold {fold+1} AUC: {fold_auc:.6f}')\n\nmeta_auc = roc_auc_score(y, meta_oof)\nprint(f'  Meta-Stack OOF AUC: {meta_auc:.6f}')\n\n# Also compute a simple weighted average as a fallback\nw_lgb = lgb_auc / (lgb_auc + xgb_auc + cat_auc)\nw_xgb = xgb_auc / (lgb_auc + xgb_auc + cat_auc)\nw_cat = cat_auc / (lgb_auc + xgb_auc + cat_auc)\n\navg_oof = w_lgb * lgb_oof + w_xgb * xgb_oof + w_cat * cat_oof\navg_test = w_lgb * lgb_test + w_xgb * xgb_test + w_cat * cat_test\navg_auc = roc_auc_score(y, avg_oof)\nprint(f'  Weighted Avg OOF AUC: {avg_auc:.6f}')\n\n# Pick the best strategy\nif meta_auc >= avg_auc:\n    final_test = meta_test_preds\n    final_auc = meta_auc\n    strategy = 'Meta-Stacking'\nelse:\n    final_test = avg_test\n    final_auc = avg_auc\n    strategy = 'Weighted Average'\n\nprint(f'\\n  BEST STRATEGY: {strategy} (AUC: {final_auc:.6f})')","metadata":{"_uuid":"0b7bc360-cb53-48af-bf7d-8aacb93750ad","_cell_guid":"3a3e2a14-fe25-479b-8f3a-cd04e25828b1","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:26:45.523366Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:26:45.523722Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:26:52.429032Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:26:45.523696Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:26:52.42819Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==============================================================================\n# DIAGNOSTICS — ROC Curves & Model Comparison\n# ==============================================================================\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 8))\n\nfor name, oof_preds, auc_score in [\n    ('LightGBM', lgb_oof, lgb_auc),\n    ('XGBoost', xgb_oof, xgb_auc),\n    ('CatBoost', cat_oof, cat_auc),\n    (f'Ensemble ({strategy})', meta_oof if strategy == 'Meta-Stacking' else avg_oof, final_auc)\n]:\n    fpr, tpr, _ = roc_curve(y, oof_preds)\n    ax.plot(fpr, tpr, linewidth=2, label=f'{name} (AUC={auc_score:.5f})')\n\nax.plot([0, 1], [0, 1], 'k--', alpha=0.3)\nax.set_xlabel('False Positive Rate', fontsize=12)\nax.set_ylabel('True Positive Rate', fontsize=12)\nax.set_title('ROC Curves — Model Comparison', fontsize=15, fontweight='bold')\nax.legend(fontsize=11)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\n# Model comparison table\nresults = pd.DataFrame({\n    'Model': ['LightGBM', 'XGBoost', 'CatBoost', strategy],\n    'OOF AUC': [lgb_auc, xgb_auc, cat_auc, final_auc]\n}).sort_values('OOF AUC', ascending=False)\nprint('\\nModel Comparison:')\nprint(results.to_string(index=False))","metadata":{"_uuid":"b96054ff-ae22-43e7-a00d-ac8c2e4314cc","_cell_guid":"112ce2df-cdef-45ad-9e96-7ab2a84dd38e","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:26:52.430122Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:26:52.430428Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:26:53.595197Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:26:52.43039Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:26:53.594521Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==============================================================================\n# SUBMISSION\n# ==============================================================================\nsubmission = pd.DataFrame({\n    'id': test['id'],\n    'addicted_label': final_test\n})\n\nprint('Submission Preview:')\nprint(submission.head(10))\nprint(f'\\nShape: {submission.shape}')\nprint(f'Prediction range: [{submission[\"addicted_label\"].min():.4f}, {submission[\"addicted_label\"].max():.4f}]')\nprint(f'Mean prediction: {submission[\"addicted_label\"].mean():.4f}')\n\n# Sanity checks\nassert len(submission) == len(sample_sub), 'Row count mismatch!'\nassert list(submission.columns) == list(sample_sub.columns), 'Column mismatch!'\nassert submission['addicted_label'].isnull().sum() == 0, 'Null predictions!'\n\nsubmission.to_csv('submission.csv', index=False)\nprint('\\nSaved submission.csv')","metadata":{"_uuid":"1d857afa-6756-4b8d-b4bb-06bcfda8abd8","_cell_guid":"6784b5d6-9289-4808-b888-89024da7ab66","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-11T22:26:53.596803Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-11T22:26:53.597147Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-11T22:26:54.164099Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-11T22:26:53.597125Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-11T22:26:54.163439Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Key Takeaways\n\n<div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0f172a,#1e1b4b);padding:25px;border-radius:15px;border:1px solid #7B68EE;color:#e2e8f0;\">\n\n### What we did:\n1. **String Trick** — Converted continuous features to categorical strings, then target-encoded them (OOF-safe). This reverse-engineers the synthetic data generator.\n2. **Minimal Feature Engineering** — Relied on raw features + target encodings. Tree models handle the signal well without manual ratios.\n3. **3-Model Diversity** — LightGBM + XGBoost + CatBoost each see the data slightly differently.\n4. **Meta-Stacking** — Used OOF predictions + polynomial interactions as features for a Logistic Regression meta-learner.\n5. **Anti-Overfitting** — 5-Fold StratifiedKFold, early stopping, OOF target encoding, and a simple meta-learner.\n\n### Generalization strategy:\n- Native missing value handling (no imputation = less noise)\n- OOF target encoding prevents train-set leakage\n- Low-variance meta-learner (LogisticRegression) on top of high-variance base models\n- Stable fold scores with low standard deviation\n\n</div>","metadata":{"_uuid":"d210a16b-b713-433e-962a-fd50c888e320","_cell_guid":"cd5afd52-b873-4a88-9e10-6c0959632cc0","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}}]}